  "critiquePairs": [
    {
      "id": "cp-1",
      "left": "no-seams",
      "right": "strong",
      "question": "A team wants messages sent to Slack. Which design lets them add that without touching the logger? Click the class they would implement.",
      "targetsConcept": "open-closed",
      "answer": {
        "design": "strong",
        "className": "Sink"
      },
      "telling": "On the right, a destination is an implementation of Sink — Slack is a new class and one line of configuration. On the left, writing to the console and to the file are methods on Logger, so Slack is a third method and an edit to log(). The brief said 'more can be added later'; that sentence is the seam."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp-2",
      "left": "fat-interface",
      "right": "strong",
      "question": "Both designs have a destination abstraction. In which one does a new destination NOT have to know how a message is laid out as text? Click the class that took that job away from destinations.",
